      "type": "subjective",
      "section": "Section B",
      "marks": 2,
      "question": "Find the multiplicative inverse of the complex number $2 - 3i$.",
      "finalAnswer": "$\\frac{2}{13} + \\frac{3}{13}i$",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$z = 2-3i$. Inverse $z^{-1} = \\frac{\\bar{z}}{|z|^2}$.",
        "$\\bar{z} = 2+3i$. $|z|^2 = 2^2 + (-3)^2 = 4+9=13$.",
        "$z^{-1} = \\frac{2+3i}{13} = \\frac{2}{13} + \\frac{3}{13}i$."
      ]
    },
